.TH TIME 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Time \- time utilities (sleep, timestamps, formatting)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Time
module provides functions for sleeping, obtaining the current time, formatting
timestamps, and decomposing timestamps into calendar components.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Sleep
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Sleep(milliseconds: int())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Blocks the current thread for the given number of milliseconds.
Uses \fBstd::this_thread::sleep_for\fR.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR \- if not exactly 1 argument.
.SS Now
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
float() Now()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns seconds since the Unix epoch (1970-01-01 UTC) as a float.
Uses \fBstd::chrono::system_clock\fR.
.TP
\fBRETURN VALUE\fR
float() \- seconds with sub-second precision.
.SS Clock
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
float() Clock()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns milliseconds since the high-resolution clock's epoch.
Suitable for benchmarking elapsed time; epoch is implementation-defined.
.SS Format
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() Format(timestamp: float(), formatStr: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Formats a Unix timestamp as a local-time string using
.BR strftime (3)
conventions.
.TP
\fBARGUMENTS\fR
.TP
timestamp (float())
Unix timestamp in seconds.
.TP
formatStr (string())
strftime format string, e.g. "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S".
.TP
\fBRETURN VALUE\fR
string() \- formatted date/time, up to 79 characters.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
Format(Now(), "%Y-%m-%d")   -> "2026-07-15"
.EE
.SS Local
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
dict() Local(timestamp: float())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Decomposes a Unix timestamp into local-time calendar components.
Returns a dict with keys:
.B year, month, day, weekday, hour, min, sec
(all int()).
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
Local(0.0)  -> {"year": 1970, "month": 1, ...}
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
System(3)
